  partName: Top Front Sensor
  description: The Top Front Sensor is a tiny, thin-flat sensor positioned at the
    top-center-front of the engine, made of Material.006, which monitors various
    engine parameters such as temperature, pressure, or speed. This sensor provides
    crucial data to the engine control unit, enabling it to adjust engine performance
    for optimal efficiency and power output. An interesting detail about the Top
    Front Sensor is that it often requires precise calibration to ensure accurate
    readings.
